:false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-05-20T14:11:22Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/1133004789","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/18649#issuecomment-1133004789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/18649","id":1133004789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAPphoM5DiEf1","user":{"login":"famiu","id":29580810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTgwODEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29580810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu","html_url":"https://github.com/famiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/famiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-05-20T14:54:53Z","updated_at":"2022-05-20T15:07:25Z","body":"The issue is that `win_redr_winbar` is called without `win_grid_alloc` because `win_redr_statusline` sets `w_redr_winbar` to true, which sets `w_winbar_height` but does not call `win_grid_alloc` since `win_grid_alloc` is called before `win_redr_statusline` in `update_screen`. Since `win_grid_alloc` is responsible for setting the `row_offset` of the grid, it causes `grid_adjust` to not adjust the grid correctly and causes the error. The fix would be to call `win_grid_alloc` somewhere in between `win_redr_statusline` and `win_redr_winbar`, what do you think is the ideal place for that?","author_as